<%# locals: (pagy:, frame: nil) -%>
<%# The one place pagy.series_nav is called. Two surfaces rendered it with
    different arguments — the shared pagination partial plain, the operations
    ledger with a hand-written `anchor_string` so its links escape the Turbo
    frame — which is one call with two spellings and no way to keep them
    honest (#1169).

    `frame:` is the seam: absent, the pager behaves exactly as before; set,
    every link carries that frame target. `anchor_string` is pagy's raw-
    attribute hook, so the value is built with `tag.attributes` rather than
    interpolated — a frame name can then never close the attribute and add
    one of its own. -%>
<% if pagy.pages > 1 %>
  <%== pagy.series_nav(
         aria_label: t("pagination.aria_label"),
         **(frame ? { anchor_string: tag.attributes(data: { turbo_frame: frame }) } : {})
       ) %>
<% end %>
